  <!-- Column 2 Text -->
  <div slot="col-2-text">
    <p>
      December was fresh and open,<br>
      And January was quite mild;<br>
      Mostly dry and sunny days,<br>
      Although gale force winds were wild.<br>
      Our seasons are all changing,<br>
      Some days it feels like spring;<br>
      The sunshine is now warming up,<br>
      And the birds are on the wing.<br>
      To be outdoors is tempting,<br>
      Yes! optimists may be forgiven;<br>
      For thinking winter is at an end,<br>
      Cast your mind back to 1947.<br>
      After a mild start in January,<br>
      Came blocked roads for weeks on end;<br>
      Snow seemingly piled up to the sky,<br>
      It nearly drove folk round the bend!<br>
      ‘This won’t happen now’ the experts say,<br>
      New equipment will keep roads clear;<br>
      But no human hand is able to,<br>
      When storms unexpectedly appear.<br>
      A higher power is in control,<br>
      And we must accept what comes;<br>
      And like the birds be grateful,<br>
      For the day’s we’re given crumbs.<br>
      Check the months on the calendar,<br>
      Spring will come in its own time;<br>
      All the sweeter for the waiting,<br>
      And bringing an end to this rhyme.<br>
      By Eila Webster
    </p>
  </div>

